          "citations": null,
          "text": "## What's happening with August revenue\n\nOverall, August's total revenue was only slightly below average (~\u20112%), but that masks a very lopsided story once you break it down by region/channel \u2014 the dataset only has one region+channel combo each per region (North=Organic, South=Paid, West=Organic), so this is really a story about **South (Paid channel)**.\n\n**North and West actually had a good August:**\n- North (Organic): revenue $82,820 vs. a ~$79,526 average the rest of the year (+4%)\n- West (Organic): revenue $69,700 vs. a ~$67,101 average (+3.9%)\n\n**South (Paid) is the problem:**\n- Revenue fell to $55,300 in August \u2014 its lowest point of the year, down ~15% from its ~$65,340 average for other months, and well below even its worst other month (January, $56,880).\n- Customers and orders in South/Paid weren't unusually low \u2014 the drop is driven by **avg order value collapsing to $70**, versus a typical range of $79\u201385 in every other month. That's the single lowest AOV recorded anywhere in the dataset.\n- At the same time, **support tickets nearly doubled** \u2014 210 in August vs. a normal range of 105\u2013121 for South/Paid in other months (and vs. ~90-105 tickets typical elsewhere in the business). This is by far the largest anomaly in the whole dataset (support tickets overall were up 40% in August, almost entirely due to this one segment).\n\n**Interpretation:** August's revenue dip isn't a broad, company-wide slowdown \u2014 customer counts and order volumes were actually fine or even up. It's concentrated in the South region's Paid channel, where something caused customers to spend noticeably less per order (AOV down ~15-17%) while generating roughly double the normal support ticket volume. That combination \u2014 lower order values plus a spike in support complaints \u2014 strongly suggests an operational issue in that specific channel/region during August: e.g., a pricing/discount problem, a promotion that devalued orders, a checkout/fulfillment glitch, or a product/service issue that both cut spending and drove customers to contact support.\n\n**Recommendation:** Pull the raw South/Paid support tickets from August to see what customers were complaining about \u2014 that should point directly to the root cause (pricing error, shipping delays, site bug, etc.) and explain both the AOV drop and the ticket spike in one shot.",
          "type": "text"
        }
